                        <div>
                            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">Configuration</h1>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
                        Soli Proxy uses two files: <code class="text-emerald-300 text-sm bg-emerald-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">proxy.conf</code> for routing rules and <code class="text-emerald-300 text-sm bg-emerald-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">config.toml</code> for server settings. Both support hot reloading without downtime.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- ============================================================ -->
                <!-- PROXY.CONF ROUTING RULES -->
                <!-- ============================================================ -->
                <div class="mb-16 " style="transition-delay: 100ms;">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-3">
                        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 text-sm font-mono">1</span>
                        Routing Rules &mdash; proxy.conf
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6 ml-11">
                        Each line maps a source pattern to one or more backend targets using the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">-&gt;</code> arrow syntax. Rules are evaluated top-to-bottom; the first match wins.
                    </p>

                    <!-- Domain-only rules -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Domain-Only Rules</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Match requests by their <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Host</code> header. Any path on that domain is forwarded to the target.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># All traffic to example.com goes to backend on port 8080</span>
<span class="tf">example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://backend:8080</span>

<span class="tc"># Multiple domains, each with its own backend</span>
<span class="tf">api.example.com</span>   <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api-server:3000</span>
<span class="tf">admin.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://admin-panel:4000</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- External https backends -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">External HTTPS Backends</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Targets can be <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https://</code> origins. The proxy rewrites <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Host</code> to the target's own authority (matching the TLS SNI, so vhosts/CDNs accept the request) and aligns a same-origin <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Origin</code> header with it, so backends that CSRF-check Origin against the request authority keep working. Cross-site Origins are forwarded untouched. The client's host reaches the backend via <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-Host</code>.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Every proxied request &mdash; rule, app or WebSocket &mdash; carries <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-For</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Real-IP</code> (the connecting address), <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-Proto</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-Host</code> (the Host the client asked for), set by the proxy. Any <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Forwarded</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-*</code> or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Real-IP</code> header the client sent is dropped first: the proxy is the edge, and a client's claim about its own address is never passed on. The exception is a peer listed in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[server] trusted_proxies</code> (a CDN, a load balancer): its <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-For</code> chain is kept and appended to, its <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-Proto</code> kept, and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Real-IP</code> names the client found in that chain. Every request also carries an <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Request-Id</code>, returned to the client too; W3C <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">traceparent</code> passes through untouched.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Serve an external https origin under your own domain</span>
<span class="tf">mirror.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">https://origin.example.net</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Redirect rules -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Redirect Rules</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Use a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">redirect://</code> target to answer with a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">301 Moved Permanently</code> instead of proxying &mdash; typically to move a site to a new canonical domain. The request path and query string are preserved on the new origin, and the destination is always <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https://</code>. WebSocket upgrade attempts receive the same 301. ACME certificates are still issued for the source domain, so the redirect itself is served over TLS.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Move a site to a new canonical domain</span>
<span class="tc"># https://old.example.com/feed?page=2 -> 301 https://new.example.com/feed?page=2</span>
<span class="tf">old.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">redirect://new.example.com</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">If another rule on the same proxy fetches its content <em>from</em> the redirected domain (e.g. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">new.example.com -&gt; https://old.example.com</code>), the redirect creates an infinite loop &mdash; point that rule directly at the backend or app instead.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Domain + Path prefix -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Domain + Path Prefix</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Combine a domain with a path prefix to route specific URL paths on a domain to a different backend.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Only /api/* paths on app.example.com go to the API service</span>
<span class="tf">app.example.com/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:8082</span>

<span class="tc"># Everything else on app.example.com goes to the frontend</span>
<span class="tf">app.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://frontend:3000</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Path-only rules -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Path-Only Rules (Any Domain)</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Match by URL path regardless of the host. Paths ending in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/*</code> match any subpath (prefix match). Paths without a wildcard require an exact match.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Prefix match: /api/ and all subpaths</span>
<span class="tf">/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:8090</span>

<span class="tc"># Exact match: only /health (not /health/check)</span>
<span class="tf">/health</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://monitoring:9090</span>

<span class="tc"># WebSocket route</span>
<span class="tf">/ws</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">ws://realtime:8888</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Regex rules -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Regex Rules</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Prefix the source with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">~</code> to use a regular expression. The regex is matched against the full request path.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/05">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Match versioned API paths: /v1/..., /v2/..., etc.</span>
<span class="tf">~^/v[0-9]+/.*$</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://versioned:8091</span>

<span class="tc"># Match UUID-based resource paths</span>
<span class="tf">~^/resources/[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-.*$</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://resources:8092</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3 mb-3">A regex rule's target may use the pattern's capture groups &mdash; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">$1</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">${1}</code>, or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">${name}</code> for <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">(?P&lt;name&gt;...)</code> &mdash; in its path and query; the client's query string is appended. A group that did not take part in the match expands to nothing, and naming a group the pattern does not have is a load error. Captures never reach the scheme or host, which are taken verbatim from the target.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># /users/42?tab=posts -> http://user-service:8080/users/42?tab=posts</span>
<span class="tf">~^/users/(\d+)$</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://user-service:8080/users/$1</span>

<span class="tc"># Named groups</span>
<span class="tf">~^/u/(?P&lt;id&gt;\d+)/(?P&lt;tab&gt;\w+)$</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://user-service:8080/users/${id}/${tab}</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- HTML URL Rewriting -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">HTML URL Rewriting</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">When using path prefix rules (like <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/api/* -> http://api:8090</code>), the proxy automatically rewrites URLs in HTML responses to include the prefix. This ensures assets loaded by the browser point to the correct path.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/05">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Route /api/* to backend (prefix stripped from request)</span>
<span class="tf">/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:8090</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">With the rule above, when the backend returns HTML like:</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden mt-2">
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"&gt;
&lt;script src="/app.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;form action="/submit"&gt;</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">The proxy rewrites it to:</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden mt-2">
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="/api/style.css"&gt;
&lt;script src="/api/app.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;form action="/api/submit"&gt;</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">The rewriting applies to <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">href</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">src</code>, and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">action</code> attributes in HTML responses. It also handles gzip/deflate compression transparently.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Multi-backend -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Multi-Backend (Load Balancing)</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Specify multiple backends separated by commas. Use backslash <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">\</code> at the end of a line to continue on the next line. Traffic is distributed across all targets.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Two backends on a single line</span>
<span class="tf">/app/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://b1:8080</span>, <span class="ts">http://b2:8080</span>

<span class="tc"># Line continuation with backslash for readability</span>
<span class="tf">/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://backend1:8080</span>, \
          <span class="ts">http://backend2:8080</span>, \
          <span class="ts">http://backend3:8080</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3 mb-3">Prefix a target with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">weight:N</code> (0&ndash;255, default 100) for weighted balancing; a rule with any weight uses <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@lb:weighted</code> unless it names another strategy. Weights are reduced by their common divisor and interleaved &mdash; 70:30 sends A B A A B A A B A A rather than 70 requests then 30. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">weight:0</code> drains a target: it takes no traffic while another weighted target is up, and serves only as a last resort. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@lb:round-robin</code> (the default) and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@lb:failover</code> (first available target) are the other strategies; every strategy skips a target whose circuit breaker is open.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># 70% / 30%</span>
<span class="tf">/api/heavy</span> <span class="tk">-></span> weight:70 <span class="ts">http://heavy:8080</span>, weight:30 <span class="ts">http://light:8080</span>

<span class="tc"># Drain the old backend before removing it</span>
<span class="tf">/app/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> weight:0 <span class="ts">http://old:8080</span>, weight:1 <span class="ts">http://new:8080</span>

<span class="tc"># All traffic to the first target that is up</span>
<span class="tf">/db/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://primary:8080</span>, <span class="ts">http://replica:8080</span> <span class="tt">@lb:failover</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Upstream options -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Upstream Protocols, TLS and Timeouts</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Besides <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">http://</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https://</code>, a target may be <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">h2c://host:port</code> (HTTP/2 with prior knowledge, for gRPC) or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">unix:/absolute/path.sock</code> (a Unix socket; requests keep the client's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Host</code> and are sent with the path the rule resolves, WebSocket upgrades included). <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@h2</code> makes a whole rule speak HTTP/2: ALPN <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">h2</code> to <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https://</code> targets, prior knowledge to cleartext and socket ones. gRPC works end to end: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">TE: trailers</code> reaches the upstream (every other <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">TE</code> value is dropped, and HTTP/1.1 upstreams get none) and response trailers reach the client &mdash; over HTTP/2, or over HTTP/1.1 when the upstream announces them in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Trailer</code>. On an HTTP/2 upstream the client's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Host</code> travels as <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-Host</code>, since <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Host</code> may not contradict <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">:authority</code>.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3"><code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@tls_ca:/path/ca.pem</code> trusts that CA bundle <em>instead of</em> the public roots, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@tls_sni:name</code> sends that name as SNI and verifies the certificate against it (for targets addressed by IP), and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@tls_client_cert:/cert.pem,/key.pem</code> presents a client certificate (mTLS). <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@tls_insecure</code> skips certificate verification entirely &mdash; anyone on the network path can then read and alter the traffic; the proxy logs a warning each time it loads such a rule. Files are read when the configuration loads: a missing or invalid one is a load error (a route saved through the admin API is then refused and nothing is written). Each must be a regular file of at most 1 MiB; the error names the file, and the reason goes to the log only, so the admin API cannot be used to probe the filesystem. Paths cannot hold whitespace or control characters. Rules with the same options share one client and its connection pool, and WebSocket upgrades to the rule's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https://</code> target use the same TLS settings (over HTTP/1.1, whatever <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@h2</code> says).</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3"><code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@timeout:120s</code> replaces <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[limits] request_timeout</code> (time to the response headers) for the rule; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@connect_timeout:2s</code> replaces the 5&nbsp;s connect timeout. Durations take a unit: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">500ms</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">2s</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">5m</code>.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># gRPC over cleartext HTTP/2, two instances, probed every 5 s</span>
<span class="tf">grpc.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">h2c://10.0.0.7:50051</span>, <span class="ts">h2c://10.0.0.8:50051</span> <span class="tt">@health:/healthz</span> <span class="tt">@health_interval:5s</span>

<span class="tc"># Internal PKI, addressed by IP, with a client certificate</span>
<span class="tf">billing.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">https://10.0.0.9:8443</span> <span class="tt">@tls_ca:/etc/soli-proxy/internal-ca.pem</span> \
                      <span class="tt">@tls_sni:billing.internal</span> <span class="tt">@tls_client_cert:/etc/soli-proxy/proxy.pem,/etc/soli-proxy/proxy.key</span>

<span class="tc"># An app listening on a Unix socket; slow reports get two minutes</span>
<span class="tf">app.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">unix:/run/app/puma.sock</span>
<span class="tf">app.example.com/reports/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">unix:/run/app/puma.sock</span> <span class="tt">@timeout:2m</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Directive</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Value</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@retries:N</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">0&ndash;10</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[upstream] retries</td><td class="py-2">Extra attempts on another target after a failure that is safe to replay.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@timeout:D</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">duration</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">request_timeout</td><td class="py-2">Time to the response headers.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@connect_timeout:D</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">duration</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">5s</td><td class="py-2">Time to establish the connection (TCP, or the socket).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@h2</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">flag</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">off</td><td class="py-2">Speak HTTP/2 to every target of the rule.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@tls_ca:/path</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">file</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">public roots</td><td class="py-2">CA bundle (PEM) that replaces the public roots.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@tls_sni:name</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">DNS name or IP</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">target host</td><td class="py-2">SNI sent and name verified.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@tls_client_cert:/c,/k</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">two files</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">none</td><td class="py-2">Client certificate and key (PEM) for mTLS.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@tls_insecure</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">flag</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">off</td><td class="py-2">No certificate verification. Avoid.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@health:/path</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">path or off</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[health_checks] default_path</td><td class="py-2">Probe each target at this path; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">off</code> opts out of the default.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">@health_interval:D</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">duration</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[health_checks] interval</td><td class="py-2">Time between probes.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">Every directive is written back as-is when the admin API rewrites <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">proxy.conf</code>. A Lua <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">on_route</code> override may send a request to an <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">h2c://</code> URL, never to a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">unix:</code> socket: a socket is only reachable as a configured target.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Per-route Lua scripts -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Per-Route Lua Scripts</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Append <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@script:filename.lua</code> to attach Lua scripts to specific routes. Multiple scripts are comma-separated.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Single script on a route</span>
<span class="tf">/admin/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://admin:4000</span> <span class="tt">@script:auth.lua</span>

<span class="tc"># Multiple scripts on a route</span>
<span class="tf">/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:3000</span> <span class="tt">@script:auth.lua,rate_limit.lua</span>

<span class="tc"># Works with multi-backend and line continuation</span>
<span class="tf">/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://a:8080</span>, \
          <span class="ts">http://b:8080</span> <span class="tt">@script:auth.lua</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Basic Auth -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">HTTP Basic Auth</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Append <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@auth:user:hash</code> to protect a route with HTTP Basic Auth. Repeat it for several accounts. Generate the bcrypt hash with the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">hash-password</code> binary shipped next to <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">soli-proxy</code>. Only bcrypt hashes at cost 4 to 13 are accepted; an entry outside that range is a load error: fatal at startup, and on a reload the previous configuration stays in force. bcrypt runs on a bounded pool off the request workers: a credential check waits up to 10&nbsp;s for a slot, and once 16 checks per slot are already queued a new one is answered <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">503</code> with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Retry-After</code>, and successes are remembered for five minutes.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3"><code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@noauth:</code> lists request paths served <em>without</em> credentials on an otherwise protected route &mdash; the escape hatch for machine-to-machine callers such as a Stripe webhook or a health probe. Entries are comma-separated and each is either an exact path (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/webhooks/stripe</code>) or a prefix ending in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">*</code> (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/hooks/*</code>, which also matches the bare <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/hooks</code>). Paths are matched before any prefix stripping, in the same canonical form rules are matched in (see below). <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@noauth</code> without <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@auth</code> or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@forward_auth:</code> does nothing; with both, it skips both.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Rules &mdash; and their <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@auth</code> / <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@noauth</code> &mdash; match a canonical form of the request path: percent-encoded unreserved characters (letters, digits, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">- . _ ~</code>) are decoded and runs of <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/</code> collapse to one, so <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">//admin/x</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/%61dmin/x</code> meet an <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/admin/*</code> rule exactly as <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/admin/x</code> does. Reserved characters stay encoded and case is not folded. The backend still receives the path as sent (a prefix rule strips its prefix from the canonical form).</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">The exemption is deliberately literal: a path carrying percent-encoding or a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">..</code> segment is never exempt, so a request cannot walk out of the carve-out into a protected path that a normalising backend would resolve differently. Anything ambiguous keeps asking for the password.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Password-protect a whole domain</span>
<span class="tf">secure.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://localhost:9000</span> <span class="tt">@auth:admin:$2b$12$...</span>

<span class="tc"># Several accounts on one route</span>
<span class="tf">staging.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://app:8080</span> <span class="tt">@auth:admin:$2b$12$...</span> <span class="tt">@auth:qa:$2b$12$...</span>

<span class="tc"># Protected domain, but the payment webhook and the health</span>
<span class="tc"># probe must reach the backend without credentials</span>
<span class="tf">app.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://app:8080</span> <span class="tt">@auth:admin:$2b$12$...</span> \
                  <span class="tt">@noauth:/webhooks/stripe,/hooks/*,/healthz</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Forward Auth -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Forward Authentication</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3"><code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@forward_auth:URL</code> lets one SSO service &mdash; oauth2-proxy, Authelia, Authentik, a Soli app &mdash; gate any route, the way Traefik's ForwardAuth, nginx's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">auth_request</code> and Caddy's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">forward_auth</code> do. Before proxying, the proxy sends the auth service a body-less <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET</code> to that URL carrying the client's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Cookie</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Authorization</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Accept</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">User-Agent</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Requested-With</code>, the proxy's own <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-For</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">-Proto</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">-Host</code>, and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-Method</code> / <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-Uri</code> describing the request.</p>
                        <ul class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3 space-y-1 list-disc ml-5">
                            <li><strong class="text-white">2xx</strong>: the request goes through. The headers named in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@forward_auth_headers:A,B</code> are copied from the answer onto the upstream request.</li>
                            <li><strong class="text-white">Anything else</strong> (401, 403, a 302 to the login page): the answer &mdash; status, headers such as <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Location</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Set-Cookie</code>, body up to 64&nbsp;KiB &mdash; goes to the client, and the upstream is never contacted.</li>
                            <li><strong class="text-white">No answer</strong> within <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[forward_auth] timeout_secs</code> (default 5&nbsp;s): <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">503</code>. Fail closed, never a pass.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">The headers named in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@forward_auth_headers:</code> are <strong class="text-white">always stripped from the client's request first</strong> &mdash; on every request, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@noauth</code> paths included &mdash; so a client cannot forge <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Auth-User</code>. Nothing is cached: a revoked session stops working on the next request. With <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@auth</code> on the same rule, Basic Auth runs first and both must pass (the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Authorization</code> header then stays with the proxy). WebSocket upgrades are gated the same way. Apps use <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[auth] forward</code> in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">app.infos</code>; in multi-tenant mode its URL must be listed in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[forward_auth] allowed_urls</code>, since the proxy fetches it.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># oauth2-proxy (--upstream=static://202 --set-xauthrequest) on :4180</span>
<span class="tf">auth.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://127.0.0.1:4180</span>

<span class="tf">grafana.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://127.0.0.1:3000</span> \
    <span class="tt">@forward_auth:http://127.0.0.1:4180/</span> \
    <span class="tt">@forward_auth_headers:X-Auth-Request-User,X-Auth-Request-Email</span> \
    <span class="tt">@noauth:/api/health</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Request headers -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Request Headers</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">A <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">headers {</code> block applies to the <em>rule right above it</em> and ends with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">}</code> on its own line. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Name: value</code> sets a header on the request sent upstream, replacing what the client sent; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">-Name</code> removes one. The block runs after the proxy has set <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">X-Forwarded-For</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">-Proto</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">-Host</code>, so it can override those too. Values may use <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">$client_ip</code> (the TCP peer, or the client a trusted proxy names; never an untrusted client's header), <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">$scheme</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">$host</code>; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">$$</code> is a literal dollar. Hop-by-hop and framing headers (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Connection</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Transfer-Encoding</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Content-Length</code>&hellip;) cannot be set. Blocks apply to WebSocket upgrades too (an upgrade is an ordinary request until the backend&rsquo;s 101); app-managed domains are not affected.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tf">api.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:3000</span>
<span class="tk">headers {</span>
    X-Real-IP: $client_ip
    X-Forwarded-Proto: $scheme
    -X-Debug-Token
<span class="tk">}</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">Any line the parser does not understand &mdash; an unknown directive, a bad <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">weight:</code>, a malformed <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@auth</code>, an unclosed block &mdash; is an error naming its line number: fatal at startup, and on a hot reload the previous rules stay in force. Earlier versions skipped such lines.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Global scripts -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Global Scripts</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">The <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[global]</code> directive applies Lua scripts to every request, regardless of the matched route.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># These scripts run on every request</span>
<span class="tk">[global]</span> <span class="tt">@script:cors.lua,logging.lua</span>

<span class="tc"># Routes follow as normal</span>
<span class="tf">/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:3000</span> <span class="tt">@script:auth.lua</span>
<span class="tf">default</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://localhost:8080</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Default fallback -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Default Fallback</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">The <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">default</code> rule catches any request that did not match a previous rule. Place it at the end of your config.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Catch-all fallback (must be last)</span>
<span class="tf">default</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://localhost:8080</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Full example -->
                    <div class="ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Complete Example</h3>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">proxy.conf</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Global middleware</span>
<span class="tk">[global]</span> <span class="tt">@script:cors.lua,logging.lua</span>

<span class="tc"># Domain-based routing</span>
<span class="tf">api.example.com</span>    <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:3000</span> <span class="tt">@script:auth.lua</span>
<span class="tf">admin.example.com</span>  <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://admin:4000</span> <span class="tt">@script:auth.lua</span>
<span class="tf">cdn.example.com</span>    <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://static:8080</span>

<span class="tc"># Domain + path prefix</span>
<span class="tf">app.example.com/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://api:3000</span>
<span class="tf">app.example.com</span>       <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://frontend:8080</span>

<span class="tc"># Path-only with load balancing</span>
<span class="tf">/api/*</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://backend1:8080</span>, \
          <span class="ts">http://backend2:8080</span>, \
          <span class="ts">http://backend3:8080</span>

<span class="tc"># Regex for versioned endpoints</span>
<span class="tf">~^/v[0-9]+/.*$</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://versioned:8091</span>

<span class="tc"># WebSocket</span>
<span class="tf">/ws</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">ws://realtime:8888</span>

<span class="tc"># External https backend (Host/Origin rewritten to the target)</span>
<span class="tf">mirror.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">https://origin.example.net</span>

<span class="tc"># Permanent redirect to a new canonical domain</span>
<span class="tf">old.example.com</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">redirect://new.example.com</span>

<span class="tc"># Catch-all fallback</span>
<span class="tf">default</span> <span class="tk">-></span> <span class="ts">http://localhost:8080</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Rule matching order info box -->
                    <div class="mt-8 ml-11 rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/5 border border-cyan-500/20 p-5">
                        <div class="flex gap-3">
                            <div class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">
                                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-cyan-300 mb-1">Matching Order</h4>
                                <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Rules are evaluated top-to-bottom. The first rule that matches the incoming request wins. Place more specific rules (domain + path, regex) before broader ones (domain-only, default). The <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">default</code> rule should always be last.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- ============================================================ -->
                <!-- CONFIG.TOML REFERENCE -->
                <!-- ============================================================ -->
                <div class="mb-16 " style="transition-delay: 200ms;">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-3">
                        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 text-sm font-mono">2</span>
                        Server Settings &mdash; config.toml
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8 ml-11">
                        The <code class="text-emerald-300 text-sm bg-emerald-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">config.toml</code> file controls server behavior, TLS, admin API, scripting, and more. All sections are optional with sensible defaults.
                    </p>

                    <!-- [server] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[server]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Core server binding and threading options.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[server]</span>
<span class="tf">bind</span> = <span class="ts">"0.0.0.0:80"</span>            <span class="tc"># HTTP listen address</span>
<span class="tf">https_port</span> = <span class="tn">443</span>               <span class="tc"># HTTPS listen port</span>
<span class="tf">worker_threads</span> = <span class="ts">"auto"</span>        <span class="tc"># "auto" = num CPUs, or a number</span>
<span class="tf">allow_encoded_slash</span> = <span class="tk">false</span>     <span class="tc"># let %2F through (GitLab-style API paths)</span>
<span class="tf">shutdown_grace_period</span> = <span class="tn">10</span>      <span class="tc"># seconds in-flight requests get on stop/restart</span>
<span class="tf">trusted_proxies</span> = [<span class="ts">"cloudflare"</span>]  <span class="tc"># whose X-Forwarded-For to believe</span>
<span class="tf">real_ip_header</span> = <span class="ts">"X-Forwarded-For"</span>  <span class="tc"># or "CF-Connecting-IP", "X-Real-IP"</span>
<span class="tf">proxy_protocol</span> = <span class="ts">"off"</span>        <span class="tc"># "v1", "v2", "any", or { https = "v2" }</span>
<span class="tf">request_id_header</span> = <span class="ts">"X-Request-Id"</span>  <span class="tc"># "" = off</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">bind</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"0.0.0.0:80"</td><td class="py-2">Address and port for HTTP</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">https_port</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">443</td><td class="py-2">Port for the HTTPS/TLS listener, on the same address as <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">bind</code>. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">bind = "[::]:80"</code> gives dual-stack (IPv6 and IPv4) listeners on both ports.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">worker_threads</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"auto"</td><td class="py-2">Tokio worker thread count</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">allow_encoded_slash</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Request paths with a dot segment (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">/api/../admin</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">%2e%2e</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">..;</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">..\</code>) are answered 400 before any rule matches, and so is an encoded slash (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">%2F</code>) anywhere. Set to <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">true</code> for backends whose API paths carry <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">%2F</code> as data (GitLab's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">group%2Fproject</code>, S3-style keys); <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">..%2F</code> stays rejected.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">shutdown_grace_period</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">10</td><td class="py-2">On SIGTERM/SIGINT the proxy stops accepting, closes idle connections (HTTP/2 gets GOAWAY) and gives in-flight requests up to this many seconds to finish &mdash; the wait ends with the last one. Then it exits, leaving managed apps running for the next proxy to adopt unless <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">[apps] stop_on_shutdown = true</code> (the default under <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">--dev</code>). At most 3600. A second signal exits at once.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">trusted_proxies</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">array</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[]</td><td class="py-2">Peers whose forwarding headers are believed: CIDRs, addresses, or the presets <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"cloudflare"</code> (Cloudflare's published ranges, compiled in), <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"private"</code> (RFC 1918, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">fc00::/7</code>) and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"loopback"</code>. From such a peer the client is found by walking <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">X-Forwarded-For</code> right to left past trusted hops; it is then used for rate limits, logs, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">X-Real-IP</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">$client_ip</code> and Lua's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">req.client_ip</code>, the chain is appended to and its <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">X-Forwarded-Proto</code> kept. A forwarded loopback, link-local or unspecified address is never believed: the peer is the client then. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">/metrics</code> is judged on the connection, never on a forwarded claim. With <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">multi_tenant</code> on, do not list loopback or Docker's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">172.16.0.0/12</code> / <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">192.168.0.0/16</code> (the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"private"</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"loopback"</code> presets): tenants connect from there, and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">soli-proxy check</code> warns. Other peers: unchanged. Trusted peers are exempt from <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_connections_per_ip</code>. Follows hot reloads.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">real_ip_header</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"X-Forwarded-For"</td><td class="py-2">Where a trusted peer names the client: the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">X-Forwarded-For</code> chain, or a single-address header such as <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">CF-Connecting-IP</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">X-Real-IP</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">True-Client-IP</code> (removed from requests by untrusted peers).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">proxy_protocol</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string or table</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"off"</td><td class="py-2">PROXY protocol on the listeners: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"v1"</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"v2"</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"any"</code>, or per listener <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">{ http = "off", https = "v2" }</code>. Read before TLS/HTTP (5 s, 1 KiB at most), only from <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">trusted_proxies</code> &mdash; any other connection is closed. The carried address is the connection's peer, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_connections_per_ip</code> included. Needs a non-empty <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">trusted_proxies</code>.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">request_id_header</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"X-Request-Id"</td><td class="py-2">Header carrying the request ID, sent upstream, returned to the client, in the access log and Lua's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">req.request_id</code>. Kept from a trusted peer when 1&ndash;128 visible ASCII characters, otherwise 32 random hex digits. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">""</code> turns request IDs off.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [tls] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[tls]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">TLS mode and certificate storage.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[tls]</span>
<span class="tf">mode</span> = <span class="ts">"auto"</span>                       <span class="tc"># "auto" = self-signed dev certs</span>
                                     <span class="tc"># "letsencrypt" = ACME production certs</span>
<span class="tf">cache_dir</span> = <span class="ts">"./certs"</span>               <span class="tc"># Directory to store certificates</span>
<span class="tf">force_https</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>                  <span class="tc"># Redirect HTTP→HTTPS with 308</span>
<span class="tf">hsts_max_age_seconds</span> = <span class="tn">63072000</span>     <span class="tc"># HSTS max-age (default 2y, 0 disables)</span>
<span class="tf">hsts_include_subdomains</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>      <span class="tc"># Append `; includeSubDomains` directive</span>
<span class="tf">min_version</span> = <span class="ts">"1.2"</span>                 <span class="tc"># or "1.3"</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">mode</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"auto"</td><td class="py-2">"auto" for self-signed, "letsencrypt" for ACME</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">cache_dir</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"./certs"</td><td class="py-2">Certificate storage directory. Cert files: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">&lt;domain&gt;.cert.pem</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">.key.pem</code>; wildcard: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">_wildcard.&lt;parent&gt;.cert.pem</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">.key.pem</code>.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">force_https</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">true</td><td class="py-2">Send a 308 to <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">https://</code> for plaintext requests.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">hsts_max_age_seconds</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">u64</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">63072000</td><td class="py-2">HSTS <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">max-age</code>. Set to 0 to omit the header entirely.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">hsts_include_subdomains</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">true</td><td class="py-2">Set to <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">false</code> on apex domains that serve independent subdomains.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">min_version</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"1.2"</td><td class="py-2">Lowest TLS version accepted, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"1.2"</code> or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"1.3"</code>. Session resumption is always on: TLS 1.3 session tickets (keys rotate every 6 hours, in memory only) and a 32k-entry TLS 1.2 session cache, so returning clients skip the full handshake.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [letsencrypt] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[letsencrypt]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">ACME / Let's Encrypt settings. Only used when <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">tls.mode = "letsencrypt"</code>.</p>
