                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[letsencrypt]</span>
<span class="tf">staging</span> = <span class="tn">false</span>               <span class="tc"># true = use staging ACME server (for testing)</span>
<span class="tf">email</span> = <span class="ts">"admin@example.com"</span>   <span class="tc"># Contact email for certificate notifications</span>
<span class="tf">terms_agreed</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>          <span class="tc"># You must agree to the ACME ToS</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">staging</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Use Let's Encrypt staging for testing</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">email</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">--</td><td class="py-2">Contact email for ACME notifications</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">terms_agreed</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">--</td><td class="py-2">Accept the ACME Terms of Service</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [admin] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[admin]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">REST Admin API for runtime management. See the <a href="/docs/admin-api" class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline underline-offset-2">Admin API docs</a> for endpoints.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[admin]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>                <span class="tc"># Enable the admin API</span>
<span class="tf">bind</span> = <span class="ts">"127.0.0.1:9090"</span>       <span class="tc"># Admin API listen address (loopback by default)</span>
<span class="tf">api_key</span> = <span class="ts">"your-secret-key"</span>   <span class="tc"># Optional: require X-API-Key header</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">enabled</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Enable or disable the admin API</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">bind</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"127.0.0.1:9090"</td><td class="py-2">Address and port for admin API</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">api_key</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string?</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">none</td><td class="py-2">If set, all requests require X-API-Key header</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [circuit_breaker] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[circuit_breaker]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Tracks backend health and stops sending traffic to failing backends. When all targets for a route are open, returns 503 Service Unavailable.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[circuit_breaker]</span>
<span class="tf">failure_threshold</span> = <span class="tn">5</span>        <span class="tc"># Consecutive failures before opening</span>
<span class="tf">recovery_timeout_secs</span> = <span class="tn">30</span>   <span class="tc"># Seconds before probing an open backend</span>
<span class="tf">success_threshold</span> = <span class="tn">2</span>        <span class="tc"># Successful probes needed to close</span>
<span class="tf">failure_status_codes</span> = [<span class="tn">502</span>, <span class="tn">503</span>, <span class="tn">504</span>]  <span class="tc"># HTTP codes that count as failures</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">failure_threshold</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">5</td><td class="py-2">Failures before breaker opens</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">recovery_timeout_secs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">30</td><td class="py-2">Seconds to wait before half-open probe</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">success_threshold</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">2</td><td class="py-2">Successes needed to close breaker</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">failure_status_codes</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">array</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[502, 503, 504]</td><td class="py-2">HTTP status codes treated as failures</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [upstream] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[upstream]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Retrying a request on another target when an attempt fails before any response byte. A <strong>connect failure</strong> (refused, unreachable, connect timeout, TLS handshake) is always safe &mdash; nothing reached the backend &mdash; so any request is retried, its body included. <strong>Any other failure</strong> (a reset, a connection closed mid-request), or a status listed in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">retry_on</code>, is retried only for idempotent methods (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET HEAD OPTIONS PUT DELETE TRACE</code>) without a body. The retry goes to the rule's next available target in rule order; for a managed app, to its other slot while a blue/green deploy has one running (and the failed slot is failed over at once); for a cluster-pushed domain, to another instance. A request a Lua hook routed is never retried elsewhere. Every failed attempt still counts in the circuit breaker. A rule with several targets keeps a copy of the request head for a possible retry; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">retries = 0</code> (or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@retries:0</code>) avoids that cost.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[upstream]</span>
<span class="tf">retries</span> = <span class="tn">1</span>                       <span class="tc"># 0 = off; @retries:N per route</span>
<span class="tf">retry_on</span> = [<span class="ts">"connect"</span>, <span class="ts">"error"</span>]   <span class="tc"># may add "500", "502", "503", "504"</span>
<span class="tf">try_duration</span> = <span class="ts">"5s"</span>              <span class="tc"># no new attempt after this long</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">retries</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">1</td><td class="py-2">Further attempts, each on a different target (at most 10).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">retry_on</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">array</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">["connect", "error"]</td><td class="py-2">Failures that are retried: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">connect</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">error</code> (alias <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">reset</code>), and statuses <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">500</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">502</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">503</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">504</code>.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">try_duration</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">duration</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">none</td><td class="py-2">Stop retrying this long after the first attempt; the request timeout bounds it anyway.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [health_checks] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[health_checks]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Active checks for <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">proxy.conf</code> targets (managed apps have their own monitor). A rule opts in with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@health:/path</code>; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">default_path</code> checks every rule except those saying <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@health:off</code>. A background task probes each distinct target (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET</code> with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">User-Agent: soli-proxy-health-check</code>, through the rule's own TLS/HTTP/2/socket settings); any answer below 500 counts as up. A target that fails <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">unhealthy_threshold</code> probes in a row is skipped by every strategy, like an open circuit breaker, until it passes <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">healthy_threshold</code> in a row. The probes follow every reload: removed checks stop, and their targets' verdicts are forgotten. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /api/v1/circuit-breaker</code> reports <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">"health": "up"</code> or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">"down"</code> for checked targets.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[health_checks]</span>
<span class="tf">default_path</span> = <span class="ts">"/healthz"</span>    <span class="tc"># omit: only rules with @health: are checked</span>
<span class="tf">interval</span> = <span class="ts">"10s"</span>
<span class="tf">timeout</span> = <span class="ts">"2s"</span>
<span class="tf">unhealthy_threshold</span> = <span class="tn">3</span>
<span class="tf">healthy_threshold</span> = <span class="tn">2</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">default_path</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">none</td><td class="py-2">Health path probed on every rule's targets.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">interval</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">duration</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">10s</td><td class="py-2">Time between probes (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@health_interval</code> per rule).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">timeout</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">duration</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">2s</td><td class="py-2">A probe without an answer by then failed.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">unhealthy_threshold</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">3</td><td class="py-2">Consecutive failed probes before a target is taken out.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">healthy_threshold</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">2</td><td class="py-2">Consecutive good probes before it is put back.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [scripting] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[scripting]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Lua 5.4 scripting engine. See the <a href="/docs/scripting" class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline underline-offset-2">Scripting docs</a> for hook details.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[scripting]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>                <span class="tc"># Enable Lua scripting engine</span>
<span class="tf">scripts_dir</span> = <span class="ts">"./scripts/lua"</span>  <span class="tc"># Directory containing Lua scripts</span>
<span class="tf">hook_timeout_ms</span> = <span class="tn">10</span>         <span class="tc"># Max execution time per hook (ms)</span>
<span class="tf">exposed_env</span> = [<span class="ts">"BACKEND_TOKEN"</span>] <span class="tc"># Variables Lua's env module may read</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">enabled</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Enable or disable scripting engine</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">scripts_dir</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"./scripts/lua"</td><td class="py-2">Path to Lua script files</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">hook_timeout_ms</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">10</td><td class="py-2">Max execution time per hook call</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">exposed_env</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">array</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[]</td><td class="py-2">Environment variables the Lua <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">env</code> module may read; any other name reads <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">nil</code>. Scripts are loaded at startup; changing them needs a restart.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [logging] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[logging]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">The proxy's own log. Every line is written by a background thread (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">tracing_appender::non_blocking</code>), so a slow disk never stalls a request; if that thread falls far behind, lines are dropped rather than blocking. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">level</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">format</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">output</code> are read at startup; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">log_endpoints</code> follows hot reloads.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[logging]</span>
<span class="tf">level</span> = <span class="ts">"info"</span>                <span class="tc"># trace, debug, info, warn, error, or a filter</span>
<span class="tf">format</span> = <span class="ts">"json"</span>               <span class="tc"># "json" or "text"</span>
<span class="tf">output</span> = <span class="ts">"stdout"</span>             <span class="tc"># "stdout", "stderr" or "file:/var/log/soli-proxy/proxy.log"</span>
<span class="tf">max_size</span> = <span class="ts">"100MB"</span>            <span class="tc"># file output: rotate past this size ("0" = never)</span>
<span class="tf">max_files</span> = <span class="tn">5</span>                 <span class="tc"># file output: rotated files kept</span>
<span class="tf">log_endpoints</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>          <span class="tc"># one line per request</span>
<span class="tf">access_log</span> = <span class="ts">"/var/log/soli-proxy/access.log"</span>  <span class="tc"># "off", "stdout", "stderr" or a path</span>
<span class="tf">access_log_format</span> = <span class="ts">"json"</span>    <span class="tc"># or "combined"</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">level</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"info"</td><td class="py-2">Verbosity: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">trace</code>&hellip;<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">error</code>, or a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">tracing</code> filter such as <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">info,soli_proxy::server=debug</code>. When unset, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">RUST_LOG</code> is used, then <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">info</code>. An invalid value stops startup.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">format</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"json"</td><td class="py-2"><code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">json</code> (one object per line; the TUI error screen reads it) or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">text</code>.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">output</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"stdout"</td><td class="py-2"><code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">stdout</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">stderr</code> or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">file:/path</code>. With <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">-d</code>, stdout/stderr mean <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">${SOLI_LOG_DIR:-.}/proxy.log</code>.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_size</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"100MB"</td><td class="py-2">File output: when the file would exceed this, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">proxy.log</code> becomes <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">proxy.log.1</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">.1</code> becomes <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">.2</code>&hellip; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">"0"</code> disables rotation. New files are created <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">0640</code>.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_files</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">5</td><td class="py-2">File output: rotated files kept; the oldest beyond this is deleted.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">log_endpoints</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Log one line per request (method, host, path, status, latency).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">access_log</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"off"</td><td class="py-2">One line per request, written once the response body is sent (or abandoned): time, client IP (the real one, see <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">trusted_proxies</code>), method, host, path and query, protocol, status, bytes in (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">Content-Length</code>) and out, duration, upstream, app, request ID, user agent, referer, TLS. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">stdout</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">stderr</code> or a file path, rotated by <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_size</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_files</code>. Through a non-blocking writer that drops lines rather than slow traffic. Read at startup.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">access_log_format</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"json"</td><td class="py-2"><code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">json</code> (one object per line) or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">combined</code> (Apache/nginx combined, followed by <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">host= rt= rid= upstream= app= tls= in=</code>).</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [limits] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[limits]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Connection and request limits.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[limits]</span>
<span class="tf">max_connections</span> = <span class="tn">10000</span>      <span class="tc"># Maximum concurrent connections</span>
<span class="tf">max_connections_per_ip</span> = <span class="tn">256</span> <span class="tc"># Per client address (IPv6: per /64); 0 = off</span>
<span class="tf">max_request_size</span> = <span class="ts">"10MB"</span>    <span class="tc"># Maximum request body size</span>
<span class="tf">keep_alive_timeout</span> = <span class="tn">30</span>     <span class="tc"># Header read / idle connection timeout (seconds)</span>
<span class="tf">request_timeout</span> = <span class="tn">60</span>        <span class="tc"># Seconds to the response headers (@timeout per route)</span>
<span class="tf">websocket_idle_timeout_secs</span> = <span class="tn">300</span>
<span class="tf">websocket_max_lifetime_secs</span> = <span class="tn">3600</span>
<span class="tf">websocket_max_bytes_per_direction</span> = <span class="tn">1073741824</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_connections</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">none</td><td class="py-2">Simultaneous client connections across HTTP and HTTPS. When none is free, an accepted connection waits up to 10 s for one (then is closed) and further connections wait in the listen backlog. Read at startup.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_connections_per_ip</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">256</td><td class="py-2">Max simultaneous connections from one client address, across HTTP and HTTPS. IPv6 clients count per /64. A connection over the cap is closed on accept. Keyed on the TCP peer (or the PROXY protocol address); a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">trusted_proxies</code> peer is exempt. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">0</code> disables the cap. Read at startup.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_request_size</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">none</td><td class="py-2">Request bodies above this are refused with 413 (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">KB</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">MB</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs">GB</code> suffixes).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">keep_alive_timeout</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">none</td><td class="py-2">Seconds allowed to receive a request's headers; also closes idle keep-alive connections.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">request_timeout</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">60</td><td class="py-2">Seconds for the upstream exchange before the client gets 504. A rule's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@timeout</code> replaces it.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">websocket_idle_timeout_secs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">300</td><td class="py-2">Close a forwarded WebSocket when both directions have been silent this long.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">websocket_max_lifetime_secs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">3600</td><td class="py-2">Absolute lifetime of a forwarded WebSocket.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">websocket_max_bytes_per_direction</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">1073741824</td><td class="py-2">Close a forwarded WebSocket once either direction has carried this many bytes.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [rate_limiting] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[rate_limiting]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Global rate limiting with token bucket strategy.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[rate_limiting]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>                <span class="tc"># Enable rate limiting</span>
<span class="tf">strategy</span> = <span class="ts">"token_bucket"</span>     <span class="tc"># Rate limiting algorithm</span>
<span class="tf">requests_per_second</span> = <span class="tn">1000</span>   <span class="tc"># Sustained request rate</span>
<span class="tf">burst_size</span> = <span class="tn">2000</span>            <span class="tc"># Maximum burst above sustained rate</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">enabled</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">true</td><td class="py-2">Enable or disable rate limiting</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">strategy</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"token_bucket"</td><td class="py-2">Rate limiting algorithm</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">requests_per_second</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">1000</td><td class="py-2">Sustained request rate per second</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">burst_size</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">2000</td><td class="py-2">Max burst above sustained rate</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [compression] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[compression]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Compresses backends&rsquo; responses with gzip, brotli or zstd when the client asks for it (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Accept-Encoding</code>, q-values honoured, ties broken by <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">algorithms</code> order) and the response is eligible: no <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Content-Encoding</code> already, not 1xx/204/206/304, a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Content-Type</code> in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">types</code> other than <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">text/event-stream</code>, at least <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">min_length</code> bytes when its length is known, and no <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Cache-Control: no-transform</code>. Compressed responses lose <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Content-Length</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Accept-Ranges</code>, strong ETags become weak, and every eligible response carries <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Vary: Accept-Encoding</code>. HEAD requests and WebSockets are never compressed.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3"><strong>Off by default.</strong> Compression costs one to two orders of magnitude more CPU per text byte than passthrough, changes what caches see, and compressing pages that reflect input next to secrets is what BREACH exploits &mdash; it is a decision, not an upgrade side effect. Per route, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@compress:on</code> / <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@compress:off</code> in proxy.conf override <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">enabled</code>; per app, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">compress = false</code> in app.infos opts out. Encoding runs in 64&nbsp;KiB slices per poll and is flushed whenever the backend pauses, so streamed responses stay live. On a path-prefix mount the HTML rewrite happens first.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[compression]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>                       <span class="tc"># default false</span>
<span class="tf">algorithms</span> = [<span class="ts">"zstd"</span>, <span class="ts">"br"</span>, <span class="ts">"gzip"</span>]  <span class="tc"># preference on a tie</span>
<span class="tf">gzip_level</span> = <span class="tn">5</span>
<span class="tf">brotli_level</span> = <span class="tn">4</span>
<span class="tf">zstd_level</span> = <span class="tn">3</span>
<span class="tf">min_length</span> = <span class="tn">1024</span>
<span class="tf">types</span> = [<span class="ts">"text/*"</span>, <span class="ts">"application/json"</span>, <span class="ts">"*+json"</span>, <span class="ts">"image/svg+xml"</span>]</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">enabled</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Compress eligible responses on routes and apps that do not opt out.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">algorithms</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">list</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">["zstd", "br", "gzip"]</td><td class="py-2">Codings offered, in order of preference when a client accepts several equally. zstd first: as small as brotli 4 or gzip 5 on HTML, in a quarter to a third of the time.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">gzip_level</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">5</td><td class="py-2">1&ndash;9.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">brotli_level</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">4</td><td class="py-2">0&ndash;11. Levels above ~5 cost several times more CPU for a few percent.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">zstd_level</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">3</td><td class="py-2">1&ndash;19.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">min_length</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">1024</td><td class="py-2">Responses with a smaller Content-Length are sent as they are.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">types</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">list</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">text, JSON, JS, XML, SVG, wasm, icons, ttf/otf</td><td class="py-2">Media types compressed: exact, <code>type/*</code>, or a suffix such as <code>*+json</code>.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [error_pages] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[error_pages]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">HTML pages for the errors the proxy itself generates (502, 503, 504, 421, 401, 413, 429&hellip;), served to clients whose <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Accept</code> lists <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">text/html</code>; everyone else keeps the plain text. Files in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">dir</code>: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">502.html</code> for one status, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">4xx.html</code> / <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">5xx.html</code> for a class, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">default.html</code>, and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">maintenance.html</code>. Templates may use <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{status}}</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{reason}}</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{host}}</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{request_id}}</code>, all HTML-escaped. Pages are read at load and on reload, never per request, 64&nbsp;KiB each.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">A backend&rsquo;s own error page, a forward-auth service&rsquo;s denial (its login form) and the body of a Lua <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">deny</code> are never replaced, unless <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">intercept_upstream_errors</code> is on. An app may bring its own pages in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;site&gt;/error_pages/</code>, used first for the requests it serves (not for an apex its derived claim yields to an operator&rsquo;s rule or a pushed route); in multi-tenant mode neither the directory nor a page may be a symlink.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[error_pages]</span>
<span class="tf">dir</span> = <span class="ts">"/etc/soli-proxy/errors"</span>
<span class="tf">intercept_upstream_errors</span> = <span class="tn">false</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">dir</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">path</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">unset</td><td class="py-2">Directory holding the pages. A missing directory or a page over 64&nbsp;KiB is a configuration error.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">intercept_upstream_errors</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">bool</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Also replace 4xx/5xx responses that came from a backend.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [maintenance] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[maintenance]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">In maintenance, requests get <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">503</code> with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Retry-After</code> and a page: the app&rsquo;s <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">error_pages/maintenance.html</code> or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">public/maintenance.html</code>, then <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">maintenance.html</code> from <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[error_pages] dir</code>, then a built-in page in French or English that shows when the site is back in the visitor&rsquo;s time zone and reloads itself once it is. While an app is closed, the files of its <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">public/maintenance/</code> are served at <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/maintenance/&lt;file&gt;</code> so its own page can have a stylesheet and images. Templates may use <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{app}}</code> (the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">display_name</code> from <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">app.infos</code>, else the host), <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{message}}</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{since}}</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{{until}}</code>.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Switch it with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">soli-proxy maintenance on &lt;app&gt;|all --for 30m -m "&hellip;"</code> / <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">off</code> / <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">status</code>, with <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">M</code> on an app in the TUI, through the admin API &mdash; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">PUT /api/v1/maintenance</code> for everything, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">PUT /api/v1/apps/{name}/maintenance</code> for one app, body <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">{"enabled": true, "for_secs": 1800, "message": "..."}</code> (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">until</code> takes an RFC&nbsp;3339 time instead), persisted to <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">run/maintenance.json</code> &mdash; or by creating <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">sites/&lt;domain&gt;/maintenance.flag</code>, which deploy scripts can do without admin credentials. A window with an end reopens by itself when it passes.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">This section only holds policy. Clients in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">allow_ips</code>, paths in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">allow_paths</code>, ACME challenges and the proxy&rsquo;s own health and metrics endpoints are served as usual.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[maintenance]</span>
<span class="tf">retry_after</span> = <span class="tn">300</span>
<span class="tf">allow_ips</span> = [<span class="ts">"10.0.0.0/8"</span>, <span class="ts">"203.0.113.7"</span>]
<span class="tf">allow_paths</span> = [<span class="ts">"/up"</span>, <span class="ts">"/status/*"</span>]
<span class="tf">language</span> = <span class="ts">"auto"</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">retry_after</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">300</td><td class="py-2">Retry-After when a toggle does not set one (seconds, at most a week).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">allow_ips</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">list</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[]</td><td class="py-2">IPs or CIDRs (v4 or v6) served normally. Judged on the TCP peer address.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">allow_paths</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">list</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[]</td><td class="py-2">Exact paths, or prefixes ending in <code>*</code>, served normally. Compared literally: percent-encoded or dot-segment spellings are not let through.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">language</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">string</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">"auto"</td><td class="py-2">The built-in page&rsquo;s language: <code>auto</code> follows the browser&rsquo;s <code>Accept-Language</code> (French or English), or <code>fr</code> / <code>en</code>.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- [bots] -->
                    <div class="mb-8 ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm">[bots]</span>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Off until turned on. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">block_agents</code> refuses with a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">403</code> the user agents it names: presets <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">ai-training</code> (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, CCBot, Bytespider&hellip;), <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">ai-assistants</code> (ChatGPT-User, PerplexityBot, Amazonbot&hellip;), <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">seo</code> (AhrefsBot, SemrushBot&hellip;), <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">scanners</code> (zgrab, Nuclei, sqlmap&hellip;), or substrings. Search engines&rsquo; crawlers are in no preset. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">traps</code> bans a client that asks for <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/.env</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/wp-login.php</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/.git/</code> and the like, and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">max_404_per_minute</code> one that collects too many 404s: a banned client gets a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">403</code> on every site until the ban ends.</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Requests a page made a browser send (a <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Sec-Fetch-Site</code> other than <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">none</code>) never ban anyone, so no site can get your visitors banned with an <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;img src="/.env"&gt;</code>. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">allow_ips</code>, loopback and the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">trusted_proxies</code> are never refused. A site sets <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[bots] enabled = false</code> in its <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">app.infos</code> to opt out entirely, or <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">enabled = true</code> to opt in while it is off everywhere else; <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">traps = false</code> when it serves such paths (a WordPress), or its own <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">block_agents</code>. Bans live in memory: <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">soli-proxy bots</code> lists them, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">soli-proxy bots unban &lt;ip&gt;</code> lifts one.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[bots]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>
<span class="tf">block_agents</span> = [<span class="ts">"ai-training"</span>, <span class="ts">"scanners"</span>]
<span class="tf">traps</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>
<span class="tf">max_404_per_minute</span> = <span class="tn">60</span>
<span class="tf">ban_secs</span> = <span class="tn">3600</span>
<span class="tf">allow_ips</span> = [<span class="ts">"203.0.113.7"</span>]</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
                            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                                <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-gray-400">
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Key</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Default</th>
                                    <th class="py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
                                </tr></thead>
                                <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">enabled</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">boolean</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">true</td><td class="py-2">The master switch: <code>false</code> turns everything off, bans included, but keeps the settings. A site&rsquo;s <code>[bots] enabled</code> in its <code>app.infos</code> wins over it, both ways.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">block_agents</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">list</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[]</td><td class="py-2">User agents refused with a 403: presets or substrings of at least three characters, compared without case.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">traps</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">boolean</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">false</td><td class="py-2">Ban a client that asks for one of the trap paths (answered 404).</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">trap_paths</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">list</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">built-in</td><td class="py-2">Replaces the built-in list (<code>/.env*</code>, <code>/.git/*</code>, <code>/wp-admin/*</code>, <code>/xmlrpc.php</code>, <code>/phpmyadmin*</code>&hellip;). Exact paths, or prefixes ending in <code>*</code>.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">max_404_per_minute</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">0</td><td class="py-2">Ban a client past this many 404s in a minute. <code>0</code>: off.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">ban_secs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">integer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">3600</td><td class="py-2">How long a ban lasts, at most a week. IPv6 clients are banned by /64.</td></tr>
                                    <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-xs">allow_ips</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">list</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-500">[]</td><td class="py-2">IPs or CIDRs never refused nor banned.</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Full config.toml example -->
                    <div class="ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Complete config.toml Example</h3>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">config.toml</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tk">[server]</span>
<span class="tf">bind</span> = <span class="ts">"0.0.0.0:80"</span>
<span class="tf">https_port</span> = <span class="tn">443</span>
<span class="tf">worker_threads</span> = <span class="ts">"auto"</span>

<span class="tk">[tls]</span>
<span class="tf">mode</span> = <span class="ts">"letsencrypt"</span>
<span class="tf">cache_dir</span> = <span class="ts">"./certs"</span>

<span class="tk">[letsencrypt]</span>
<span class="tf">staging</span> = <span class="tn">false</span>
<span class="tf">email</span> = <span class="ts">"admin@example.com"</span>
<span class="tf">terms_agreed</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>

<span class="tk">[admin]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>
<span class="tf">bind</span> = <span class="ts">"127.0.0.1:9090"</span>
<span class="tf">api_key</span> = <span class="ts">"your-secret-key"</span>

<span class="tk">[circuit_breaker]</span>
<span class="tf">failure_threshold</span> = <span class="tn">5</span>
<span class="tf">recovery_timeout_secs</span> = <span class="tn">30</span>
<span class="tf">success_threshold</span> = <span class="tn">2</span>
<span class="tf">failure_status_codes</span> = [<span class="tn">502</span>, <span class="tn">503</span>, <span class="tn">504</span>]

<span class="tk">[scripting]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>
<span class="tf">scripts_dir</span> = <span class="ts">"./scripts/lua"</span>
<span class="tf">hook_timeout_ms</span> = <span class="tn">10</span>

<span class="tk">[logging]</span>
<span class="tf">level</span> = <span class="ts">"info"</span>
<span class="tf">format</span> = <span class="ts">"json"</span>
<span class="tf">output</span> = <span class="ts">"file:/var/log/soli-proxy/proxy.log"</span>
<span class="tf">max_size</span> = <span class="ts">"100MB"</span>
<span class="tf">max_files</span> = <span class="tn">5</span>

<span class="tk">[limits]</span>
<span class="tf">max_connections</span> = <span class="tn">10000</span>
<span class="tf">max_connections_per_ip</span> = <span class="tn">256</span>
<span class="tf">max_request_size</span> = <span class="ts">"10MB"</span>
<span class="tf">keep_alive_timeout</span> = <span class="tn">30</span>
<span class="tf">request_timeout</span> = <span class="tn">60</span>

<span class="tk">[rate_limiting]</span>
<span class="tf">enabled</span> = <span class="tn">true</span>
<span class="tf">strategy</span> = <span class="ts">"token_bucket"</span>
<span class="tf">requests_per_second</span> = <span class="tn">1000</span>
<span class="tf">burst_size</span> = <span class="tn">2000</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- ============================================================ -->
                <!-- HOT RELOADING -->
                <!-- ============================================================ -->
                <div class="mb-16 " style="transition-delay: 300ms;">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-3">
                        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 text-sm font-mono">3</span>
                        Hot Reloading
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8 ml-11">
                        Configuration changes are applied without restarting the proxy or dropping active connections. There are three ways to trigger a reload. Both files are parsed into a new configuration that replaces the old one in one atomic swap: requests already in flight finish under the old rules, the next request sees the new ones, and nothing is drained or closed. If either file fails to parse, the previous configuration stays in force and the error is logged.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8 ml-11">
                        A reload does <em>not</em> change what is set up at startup: listener addresses (<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">bind</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https_port</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">worker_threads</code>), the admin API's <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">enabled</code>/<code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">bind</code>, TLS certificates (use <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">POST /api/v1/certs/reload</code>) and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">min_version</code>, the Lua engine and its scripts, the rate limiter, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">max_connections</code>, and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">[logging]</code> level/format/output/access_log. Those need a restart. <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">trusted_proxies</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">real_ip_header</code>, <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">request_id_header</code> and <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">proxy_protocol</code> apply to the next request or connection. The file watcher only watches <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">proxy.conf</code>; after editing <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">config.toml</code>, send SIGUSR1 or call the admin endpoint.
                    </p>

                    <!-- Three methods grid -->
                    <div class="ml-11 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-8">
                        <!-- SIGUSR1 -->
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 p-5 hover:bg-white/5 transition-all">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400">
                                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">SIGUSR1 Signal</h4>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">Send a Unix signal to the running process for immediate reload.</p>
                            <code class="text-xs text-emerald-300 bg-emerald-500/10 px-2 py-1 rounded block">kill -USR1 $(pidof soli-proxy)</code>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Admin API -->
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 p-5 hover:bg-white/5 transition-all">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-cyan-400">
                                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 9l3 3-3 3m5 0h3M5 20h14a2 2 0 002-2V6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Admin API</h4>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">HTTP endpoint for programmatic reload from scripts or CI/CD.</p>
                            <code class="text-xs text-cyan-300 bg-cyan-500/10 px-2 py-1 rounded block">POST http://localhost:9090/api/v1/reload</code>
                        </div>

                        <!-- File Watcher -->
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 p-5 hover:bg-white/5 transition-all">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-teal-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-teal-400">
                                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"/><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M2.458 12C3.732 7.943 7.523 5 12 5c4.478 0 8.268 2.943 9.542 7-1.274 4.057-5.064 7-9.542 7-4.477 0-8.268-2.943-9.542-7z"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">File Watcher</h4>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">Automatic detection when proxy.conf is modified on disk.</p>
                            <code class="text-xs text-teal-300 bg-teal-500/10 px-2 py-1 rounded block">Automatic &mdash; no action needed</code>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- SIGUSR1 example -->
                    <div class="ml-11 mb-8">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">SIGUSR1 Signal</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Send the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">SIGUSR1</code> signal to the Soli Proxy process. This is the simplest reload method for manual operations.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">bash</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Find and signal the process</span>
<span class="tf">kill</span> <span class="tk">-USR1</span> <span class="ts">$(pidof soli-proxy)</span>

<span class="tc"># Or if using systemd</span>
<span class="tf">systemctl</span> <span class="tk">kill</span> <span class="ts">--signal=USR1</span> soli-proxy</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Admin API reload -->
                    <div class="ml-11 mb-8">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Admin API Reload</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">Call the Admin API reload endpoint. Requires the admin API to be enabled in <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">config.toml</code>.</p>
                        <div class="code-window rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                    <div class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/60"></span><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/60"></span></div>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 ml-2">bash</span>
                                </div>
                                <button onclick="copyCode(this)" class="text-xs text-gray-500 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
                            </div>
                            <pre class="p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="tc"># Without API key (loopback only): mutations need X-Requested-With</span>
<span class="tf">curl</span> <span class="tk">-X POST</span> <span class="ts">http://localhost:9090/api/v1/reload</span> \
  <span class="tk">-H</span> <span class="ts">"X-Requested-With: curl"</span>

<span class="tc"># With API key authentication</span>
<span class="tf">curl</span> <span class="tk">-X POST</span> <span class="ts">http://localhost:9090/api/v1/reload</span> \
  <span class="tk">-H</span> <span class="ts">"X-API-Key: your-secret-key"</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- File Watcher -->
                    <div class="ml-11">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Automatic File Watcher</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-3">
                            Soli Proxy watches the <code class="text-cyan-300 text-xs bg-cyan-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">proxy.conf</code> file for changes using OS-level file notifications (inotify on Linux, FSEvents on macOS). When a change is detected, configuration is reloaded automatically.
                        </p>
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/5 border border-emerald-500/20 p-5">
                            <div class="flex gap-3">
                                <div class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">
                                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-1">Smart Suppression</h4>
                                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">When routes are modified via the Admin API, the file watcher suppresses the next filesystem event to avoid a double reload. The Admin API writes to <code class="text-emerald-300 text-xs bg-emerald-500/10 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">proxy.conf</code> and swaps the in-memory config atomically.</p>
                                </div>
